I developed a Flutter-based Event Finder application that allows users to explore events dynamically fetched from a mock API.

The app consists of two main screens: a Home Screen, which displays a scrollable list of events, and an Event Detail Screen, which shows complete information about a selected event.

I integrated the API using the HTTP package and converted JSON responses into Dart models for structured data handling.

The application includes proper state management with loading, error, and empty states, and navigation between screens is implemented using Flutter’s Navigator.

To enhance user experience, I added pull-to-refresh functionality and a search bar UI.

The project follows a clean and organized architecture with separate folders for screens, models, services, and reusable widgets.
